        '6-8', $q$Shade for Main Street$q$, $q$(1) On summer afternoons, the sidewalks on Main Street in Pinecrest become so hot that many people avoid walking there, even to reach their favorite shops. (2) The town has many problems. (3) Trees cool the air around them by shading the ground and releasing water through their leaves. (4) Our county parks department measured shaded sidewalks that were up to fifteen degrees cooler than sunny ones. (5) Cooler sidewalks would bring more shoppers, which would help the small businesses on the street.

(6) Some business owners argue that tree roots could crack the sidewalks. (7) ______ city planners can choose kinds of trees whose roots grow deep instead of spreading sideways. (8) Planters with root barriers can also protect the pavement around each tree for many years.

(9) Trees would make Main Street cooler, friendlier, and better for business. (10) I think trees are pretty and stuff, so whatever.$q$, 'draft')
