insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('9f04ec37-2cc1-5125-8697-b0d505418e47', 'wg6-argument-writing-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g6-argument-writing'), null,
        '6-8', $q$Free Museum Visits for Students$q$, $q$(1) The Hollis County History Museum holds old maps, farm tools, and letters written by the people who founded our town. (2) Yet few students ever see these treasures, because a single ticket costs twelve dollars. (3) The museum should let visitors under eighteen enter for free. (4) Seeing real objects helps students understand history in a way that textbooks alone cannot. (5) A student who studies a settler's handwritten letter may remember that lesson for many years.

(6) Museum leaders might say that free tickets would cost them money they need. (7) ______ more student visitors could actually bring in more money. (8) Students who enjoy a visit often return with their parents, who pay full price. (9) Those families may also buy books, maps, or postcards at the museum shop before they leave.

(10) In conclusion, museums are fun.$q$, 'draft')
